\viewkind4\uc1\pard\li225\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0  God the Father I give Thee praise 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  And Thy glory is most high!
\par  Thou art Master look upon us
\par  from the Heavens to the earth.
\par  Thy glory and mighty power
\par  shall revealed in all nations.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   God of heaven thou art Mighty
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  Thou are more than everything.       
\par  All things on earth thou created
\par  with thy word they all appeared
\par  And thou have them all in thine hands
\par \pard       All Thy things are wonderful.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse 3\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. \cf0  Days and years, the time of the earth
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Thou arranged before they come
\par One day or but a thousand years.
\par All are one within Thy sight,
\par Nothing then can take off your life,
\par  Everlasting God Thou art.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  With Thy pow'r has Thou filled the earth; 
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  And the Heavens with thy life;
\par  And the gap between us to close 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Thou art anywhere with us.
\par  Thy spirit to us surrounded,
\par  As Your everlasting life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  God of Heaven and of the earth
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  We are Thine alway to be;
\par  Let Thy Mighty power dawn on us,
\par  That we shall serve You always.
\par  Make us to fear and to love Thee,
\par \pard     That we may see you in Heav'n\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

